<title>EGYPT: Public transport workers strike in Egypt.</title>
<headline>Public transport workers strike in Egypt.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>More than 2,000 public transport workers have gone on strike in the Egyptian Delta province of Gharbiya to protest against the cancellation of their annual bonuses, police in the province said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Security sources in the province said the strike in the provincial capital Tanta by 2,700 bus conductors, drivers and other transport workers had brought work to a standstill at the town's textile factories.</p>
<p>Workers at the factory are dependent on the bus company for transportation.</p>
<p>The strike began on Wednesday.</p>
</text>
